WEBVTT

00:20.000 --> 00:20.880
Fumika.

00:22.000 --> 00:23.550
Don't touch it.

00:23.550 --> 00:25.260
It's not moving.

00:25.260 --> 00:26.460
Because it's dead, isn't it?

00:26.760 --> 00:28.170
Dead?

00:28.170 --> 00:30.220
Yes, dead.

00:32.050 --> 00:33.260
Can it come back to life?

00:34.890 --> 00:36.470
This isn't a game, you know.

00:50.450 --> 00:50.700
The true forms

00:52.280 --> 00:52.530
Of the things that I gazed at

00:54.160 --> 00:54.410
Were for showing after I closed my eyes

00:55.290 --> 00:58.160
Shigofumi

00:57.870 --> 00:58.120
Again today, time

00:59.710 --> 00:59.960
Will only construct a loneliness

01:01.500 --> 01:01.750
That seems to be torn apart, right?

01:08.920 --> 01:09.170
There are people who can't forget about

01:12.590 --> 01:12.840
The white lotuses that bloom in the darkness

01:16.220 --> 01:16.470
Nevertheless, recollections

01:19.980 --> 01:20.230
Visit from the future

01:23.650 --> 01:23.900
Words that turn into sighs

01:31.070 --> 01:31.320
Are the emerging wings of the soul

01:34.740 --> 01:34.990
Will I flutter apart?

01:38.450 --> 01:38.700
Growing confused and disordered

01:42.120 --> 01:42.370
I want to carve

01:44.460 --> 01:44.710
These letters to you

01:49.460 --> 01:49.710
Pieces of the truth

01:51.300 --> 01:51.550
Of things that I want to tell you-

01:53.180 --> 01:53.430
I can't even send them well to you

01:56.930 --> 01:57.180
If I write them with the blood that stains my fingertips

02:00.600 --> 02:00.850
Then can they spill into your heart?

02:04.270 --> 02:04.520
Even if the one word left behind

02:07.520 --> 02:07.770
To us who live

02:10.230 --> 02:10.490
Is to be goodbye

02:19.660 --> 02:22.410
But why divorce?

02:22.410 --> 02:24.370
I heard that it was because of an affair.

02:24.370 --> 02:25.460
Which one?

02:25.460 --> 02:27.130
Get this, both of them!

02:27.130 --> 02:28.710
You don't say!

02:28.710 --> 02:32.800
What's more, it was with the brother-in-law.

02:32.800 --> 02:36.840
She really didn't seem like that kind of person.

02:36.840 --> 02:39.390
No, I'm talking about the husband.

02:39.390 --> 02:40.520
What?!

02:40.520 --> 02:41.970
Unbelievable.

02:41.970 --> 02:44.850
They say you can't judge a person from their looks, but this...

02:44.850 --> 02:46.650
Yeah, you're right.

02:46.650 --> 02:47.900
And...

03:05.500 --> 03:07.210
What are you doing, Uncle?

03:08.710 --> 03:09.920
Uncle?

03:10.550 --> 03:11.920
Oh, me?

03:12.630 --> 03:14.380
You're not going to join the others?

03:15.130 --> 03:17.390
I'm drawing a picture.

03:19.050 --> 03:20.640
But, there's nothing drawn.

03:26.640 --> 03:29.770
Well, I'm not really sure what to draw.

03:31.900 --> 03:33.030
Outside!

03:35.280 --> 03:36.820
I see!

03:36.820 --> 03:39.870
I guess I'm having trouble because
I'm limiting myself to what's inside here.

03:41.700 --> 03:43.120
Takehiko.

03:44.870 --> 03:46.540
Take care of the house, okay?

03:46.540 --> 03:47.750
Going out?

03:47.750 --> 03:50.590
Everyone is interested in seeing
the place we were talking about.

03:50.880 --> 03:52.500
So, we're going to go take a look.

03:55.260 --> 03:57.430
Sorry about this, Takehiko-san.

03:57.430 --> 03:58.430
Not at all.

03:58.970 --> 04:00.600
Be a good girl.

04:00.600 --> 04:01.930
Yes.

04:05.100 --> 04:08.230
It's true! Ninjas take your order...

04:10.480 --> 04:11.810
Looks like they've gone.

04:12.270 --> 04:13.150
Yeah.

04:27.160 --> 04:30.250
Are these all the dishes you've ordered?

04:31.210 --> 04:32.130
This good?

04:32.130 --> 04:32.840
Yep.

04:33.340 --> 04:34.460
Please enjoy yourselves.

04:35.340 --> 04:36.420
It's complete.

04:50.390 --> 04:52.770
Don't you have to work?

04:52.770 --> 04:53.730
Huh?

04:53.730 --> 04:55.610
It's Monday after all.

04:56.190 --> 04:57.780
Oh, really?

04:58.690 --> 05:02.660
You see, I drew at work.

05:03.320 --> 05:08.500
But, I suppose it was not what I wanted to draw personally.

05:09.620 --> 05:13.080
In short, I failed to get the right job.

05:09.620 --> 05:14.290
Note: Job - Referring to character class in RPGs.

05:13.080 --> 05:14.290
Job?

05:14.290 --> 05:17.630
Although you're a grown-up, you're using game lingo.

05:18.090 --> 05:19.550
Because I love games.

05:19.550 --> 05:20.970
Then, you must be good!

05:21.970 --> 05:23.180
Wanna challenge me?

05:32.400 --> 05:34.060
You're really good!

05:34.060 --> 05:37.980
It's been a while since I've played
a shooter, but I guess I'm doing pretty well.

05:38.280 --> 05:39.570
Uncle, on your right!

05:39.570 --> 05:42.030
You get a life-up if you pick up the red one.

05:49.450 --> 05:50.660
Uncle?

05:52.960 --> 05:55.040
I guess my skill has declined.

05:57.800 --> 05:58.840
Welcome.

05:58.840 --> 06:00.840
Four customers please!

06:01.630 --> 06:05.680
That reminds me, Takehiko-san
works for a game company, right?

06:05.680 --> 06:08.970
He quit all of a sudden last week though.

06:08.970 --> 06:10.100
Why?

06:10.100 --> 06:12.350
He wouldn't tell me.

06:12.350 --> 06:13.640
Geez.

06:13.640 --> 06:15.810
He's over thirty already, isn't he?

06:15.810 --> 06:17.690
And he's not married either, right?

06:17.690 --> 06:18.730
How worrying.

06:19.030 --> 06:22.190
He's been drawing and playing games all his life.

06:22.190 --> 06:23.780
I don't really understand him.

06:24.700 --> 06:26.030
Yeah.

06:26.030 --> 06:27.660
Look, a ninja has come out.

06:36.790 --> 06:39.170
Dragonman is suffering from a terminal disease?

06:39.550 --> 06:40.760
What does "terminal" mean?

06:41.460 --> 06:43.510
It means that he won't recover.

06:43.510 --> 06:45.220
How could that be?

06:45.220 --> 06:47.180
Dragonman!

06:51.680 --> 06:52.640
Cancer?

06:52.640 --> 06:57.230
Yes. To put it more accurately, it's cancer of the appendix.

06:59.980 --> 07:02.860
Um... It can be cured, can't it?

07:03.650 --> 07:04.700
It can be cured, can't it?

07:08.950 --> 07:10.830
Dragon Tornado!

07:11.120 --> 07:12.160
Dragonman!

07:12.700 --> 07:14.250
What happened to your illness?

07:14.250 --> 07:16.500
I killed it off with my Dragon Claw.

07:31.760 --> 07:33.390
Dragon Tornado!

07:37.850 --> 07:39.860
Watch where you're going, old man!

07:42.530 --> 07:44.610
What is it? Got a problem?

07:45.070 --> 07:47.150
Youngsters nowadays are dangerous, you know?

07:47.660 --> 07:49.410
They mention it in the news, right?

07:49.700 --> 07:53.080
That's right. Drawing out knives right away and all.

07:53.080 --> 07:54.870
It's like being in a game?

07:57.870 --> 07:59.080
Try it.

08:00.460 --> 08:04.010
This isn't a time to be cocky, old man!

08:06.220 --> 08:07.090
Why you!

08:08.550 --> 08:09.680
Want some?!

08:09.680 --> 08:10.890
Uncle!

08:11.180 --> 08:13.760
Don't underestimate us, old man!

08:16.930 --> 08:18.600
<i>I'm so weak.</i>

08:18.600 --> 08:20.980
<i>Like being at the level of a novice hero.</i>

08:20.980 --> 08:23.230
Stop! Please stop!

08:23.900 --> 08:25.690
<i>What am I doing?</i>

08:25.690 --> 08:27.490
<i>I'm already over thirty.</i>

08:27.490 --> 08:28.820
You punks!

08:28.820 --> 08:29.860
Oh, shit!

08:30.450 --> 08:31.820
Trying to run?!

08:33.910 --> 08:36.330
Are you all right, Missy?

08:36.330 --> 08:37.290
Yes.

08:41.330 --> 08:42.420
You saved me.

08:42.420 --> 08:43.380
It was one-sided...

08:44.630 --> 08:47.300
Do you know what you've done?

08:48.380 --> 08:50.840
How could you bring a young girl like that around?

08:52.050 --> 08:53.390
What are you saying?

08:53.390 --> 08:54.510
I was just...

08:54.810 --> 08:56.180
There's a law against this!

08:56.180 --> 08:57.810
Stop!

08:58.180 --> 09:00.310
You're charged with abducting a minor.

09:00.310 --> 09:01.810
No, you've got it wrong!

09:01.810 --> 09:04.020
Stop! He didn't do anything wrong!

09:04.320 --> 09:07.110
Deceiving a small girl like her; have you no shame?

09:12.570 --> 09:14.530
Kamome City
Police Station

09:14.870 --> 09:17.200
Hibiya Takehiko, your age?

09:17.950 --> 09:20.080
Thirty-two.

09:20.080 --> 09:21.330
Your job?

09:22.670 --> 09:23.670
I'm not working.

09:24.000 --> 09:25.500
Unemployed?

09:25.500 --> 09:27.840
You're not working at your age?

09:29.630 --> 09:32.430
Sheesh, another unemployed person?

09:32.430 --> 09:35.720
You're a fine adult, find proper employment.

09:35.720 --> 09:39.270
It's because you're not accepted
by society and have so much free time...

09:39.270 --> 09:41.640
that you're going around with other people's children.

09:41.940 --> 09:43.310
She's a relative's child.

09:44.560 --> 09:46.730
You think you can get away with that kind of excuse?!

09:47.230 --> 09:50.490
It'll be right past the sign at the intersection four blocks down.

09:50.490 --> 09:52.950
Submit it to the government office by the end of the day please.

09:52.950 --> 09:54.410
Like I said, it's theft.

09:54.990 --> 09:57.620
The person that can speak English is delayed though.

10:07.920 --> 10:09.880
Thank you.

10:09.880 --> 10:12.300
I'll never forget this.

10:13.090 --> 10:15.140
What's wrong?

10:27.150 --> 10:29.150
Shigofumi

10:30.280 --> 10:32.280
Shigofumi

10:39.660 --> 10:41.080
You're a bad guy, aren't you?

10:41.910 --> 10:43.830
Bad guy, she says.

10:45.830 --> 10:48.130
You were bullying her, weren't you?

10:48.130 --> 10:49.960
No, she wasn't.

10:49.960 --> 10:50.880
This is...

10:52.210 --> 10:56.840
This person here came to deliver an important letter to me.

10:57.260 --> 10:59.180
Postman?

10:59.180 --> 11:00.100
Yes.

11:02.100 --> 11:03.850
Are there any letters for Fumika too?

11:04.850 --> 11:06.600
She has the same name as you, doesn't she?

11:07.060 --> 11:09.480
My name is Fumika too.

11:10.440 --> 11:12.190
That's the same as me.

11:13.070 --> 11:15.650
This is the first time I've met someone with the same name.

11:16.660 --> 11:18.120
Are you certain?

11:18.410 --> 11:21.790
Was Hibiya Takehiko-san with your company?

11:23.160 --> 11:24.080
Yeah.

11:24.370 --> 11:26.540
Yes, there's no mistaking it.

11:26.540 --> 11:29.670
Hibiya Takehiko was an employee here.

11:30.250 --> 11:33.130
Can you pass me over to him, please?

11:35.590 --> 11:37.180
I've gotten confirmation.

11:37.640 --> 11:40.140
Don't do such misleading things any more.

11:40.890 --> 11:42.680
Ueno-san would like to speak with you.

11:48.690 --> 11:49.690
Hello?

11:50.650 --> 11:54.150
Sorry for getting you involved in this.

11:54.650 --> 11:56.700
<i>Why did you hand in your resignation?</i>

11:59.780 --> 12:01.830
<i>You can't tell me either?</i>

12:01.830 --> 12:04.500
<i>Even though we joined the company together?</i>

12:05.500 --> 12:06.830
Forgive me.

12:07.290 --> 12:09.420
What about the project we were going to do together?

12:09.880 --> 12:11.750
Are you telling me to do it without you?

12:12.380 --> 12:13.590
<i>Sorry.</i>

12:14.050 --> 12:17.510
You won't be able to return
if you leave the company like this.

12:17.970 --> 12:18.800
You sure about this?

12:19.930 --> 12:23.010
Yeah. I don't plan on going back.

12:23.510 --> 12:27.230
<i>Really? And I thought you were a friend.</i>

12:31.520 --> 12:33.520
Yuzawa General Hospital

12:45.620 --> 12:46.620
Fumi-chan.

12:47.120 --> 12:49.960
I met a girl with the same name as me today.

12:50.330 --> 12:52.210
She was very young.

12:52.210 --> 12:54.090
A first grader.

12:55.630 --> 12:57.550
I guess she'd be around that age.

12:58.720 --> 13:00.680
Fumika, you came.

13:00.680 --> 13:02.430
I had to make a delivery.

13:02.430 --> 13:03.680
What lies.

13:03.680 --> 13:06.060
You come here even when you don't have any deliveries.

13:09.940 --> 13:11.770
It's because I think she can hear me.

13:14.820 --> 13:18.400
Don't worry. I'm sure your voice is reaching her.

13:23.620 --> 13:25.910
We're coming from the neighbouring city right now.

13:26.370 --> 13:29.660
Fumika-chan wanted to watch a movie.

13:29.660 --> 13:29.790
I'm going to go eat
with Fumika-chan.

13:29.660 --> 13:32.120
You should have called me if you're going to be late.

13:29.910 --> 13:30.040
Takehiko

13:32.500 --> 13:34.840
<i>I called, but you were out.</i>

13:34.840 --> 13:37.050
Either way, please come home quickly.

13:37.050 --> 13:40.260
Oh, and also, I was talking with Misawa-san.

13:40.800 --> 13:43.760
<i>She said that she'll recommend you to a job.</i>

13:43.760 --> 13:47.770
<i>It's with a credit union. You'll be
starting off as a contract worker though.</i>

13:48.270 --> 13:50.100
<i>Isn't this a good opportunity?</i>

13:50.100 --> 13:54.230
<i>It's a regular job, not a strange job like making games.</i>

13:54.690 --> 13:57.190
What's "regular"?

13:57.190 --> 14:00.610
<i>I've told your father that you're
on an extended vacation at the moment.</i>

14:01.700 --> 14:05.530
<i>I just didn't have the heart to tell
your father that you're unemployed.</i>

14:05.530 --> 14:07.120
<i>And to the neighbours too.</i>

14:07.580 --> 14:10.540
I see. So, image in society is important?

14:10.540 --> 14:12.830
<i>I didn't say that.</i>

14:12.830 --> 14:14.120
You are saying it.

14:14.120 --> 14:17.210
Mum, you've always disliked the fact that I'm an otaku.

14:18.590 --> 14:21.260
You've always wanted a more normal kid, right?

14:22.220 --> 14:24.430
Getting into a normal company.

14:24.430 --> 14:26.260
Marry like normal.

14:26.760 --> 14:29.220
And have grandchildren for you like normal.

14:30.220 --> 14:31.680
<i>Takehiko...</i>

14:32.730 --> 14:34.770
But, I...

14:48.700 --> 14:49.790
Uncle.

14:49.790 --> 14:50.240
Hm?

14:50.240 --> 14:52.870
Let's go to that ninja place next time.

14:53.370 --> 14:54.670
Ninja?

14:54.670 --> 14:56.380
The one Mummy and her friends were talking about.

14:57.630 --> 15:01.380
We can't go there. That place serves alcohol.

15:01.880 --> 15:04.130
How unfair, everything is for adults.

15:04.430 --> 15:06.550
Are you jealous of adults?

15:06.550 --> 15:07.390
Yep.

15:08.430 --> 15:11.850
It's not that great being an adult.

15:17.230 --> 15:18.270
What is it?

15:31.410 --> 15:32.950
It won't run?

15:32.950 --> 15:35.080
Yeah, she's a goner.

15:35.540 --> 15:37.960
And I don't think any cars will be passing.

15:38.250 --> 15:40.340
Can you wait here?

15:40.340 --> 15:42.460
I'll go call for help.

15:43.760 --> 15:46.840
Don't move from here, okay?

15:54.310 --> 15:57.190
<i>I've lost everything.</i>

15:58.150 --> 16:02.400
<i>My job, friends, parents...</i>

16:02.980 --> 16:04.150
<i>Even my luck.</i>

16:05.940 --> 16:07.570
<i>I guess it doesn't matter.</i>

16:08.950 --> 16:10.700
<i>Soon, even my life too.</i>

16:18.540 --> 16:20.130
Let's go together.

16:20.920 --> 16:22.000
With me?

16:22.000 --> 16:22.790
Yep.

16:23.920 --> 16:26.340
You'll go together with me?

16:26.340 --> 16:28.630
I don't want to be alone.

16:29.090 --> 16:32.350
I see. No one likes being alone, right?

16:32.350 --> 16:33.560
It's lonely, isn't it?

16:34.100 --> 16:35.020
Yep.

16:36.810 --> 16:37.770
Fumika-chan.

16:42.690 --> 16:44.860
Wait, I have to feed him.

16:45.730 --> 16:46.690
Feed?

16:46.990 --> 16:49.150
It's a game, Forest Friends.

16:50.110 --> 16:53.660
Do you know? There are animals living inside.

16:54.080 --> 16:57.040
Look! I'm best friends with this one.

16:58.500 --> 17:00.120
<i>That's right...</i>

17:00.120 --> 17:02.500
<i>I drew that.</i>

18:21.750 --> 18:24.580
<i>I wanted to draw.</i>

18:26.540 --> 18:30.420
<i>That's why I joined a game company as a graphic artist.</i>

18:35.220 --> 18:36.390
<i>What kind of art?</i>

18:37.550 --> 18:38.930
<i>No, that's not it.</i>

18:43.440 --> 18:44.440
<i>I just...</i>

18:45.150 --> 18:51.400
<i>wanted to draw and make people happy.</i>

19:04.210 --> 19:05.460
<i>I see.</i>

19:05.960 --> 19:07.630
<i>It did come true.</i>

19:08.670 --> 19:09.880
<i>This isn't bad.</i>

19:11.250 --> 19:14.970
<i>I guess this isn't bad at all, in a sense.</i>

19:21.060 --> 19:23.390
Funeral
Hall
for the
Hibiya
Family

19:23.390 --> 19:25.100
Relatives

19:25.100 --> 19:25.230
Relatives

19:25.230 --> 19:27.440
Relatives

19:40.030 --> 19:41.990
He protected a girl.

19:41.990 --> 19:44.660
He was a kind-hearted person.

19:45.290 --> 19:47.420
But, I can't believe he was in the final stage of cancer.

19:48.000 --> 19:49.580
Then, this was just another way to go.

20:10.650 --> 20:12.900
Uncle, are you sleeping?

20:13.400 --> 20:15.030
It's noontime already.

20:15.490 --> 20:17.150
Everyone is watching, you know.

20:18.660 --> 20:20.240
Come on, Uncle...

20:39.010 --> 20:40.510
You're the girl from that day.

20:43.680 --> 20:44.850
A letter?

20:45.350 --> 20:46.640
A Shigofumi.

20:47.140 --> 20:48.810
Shigo...

20:48.810 --> 20:50.100
What does that mean?

20:55.780 --> 20:55.820
Thank
you

20:56.650 --> 21:00.240
The final miracle consented to men.

21:08.500 --> 21:10.210
Say, Miss...

21:13.420 --> 21:15.300
Did Uncle die?

21:15.800 --> 21:16.710
Yes.

21:19.420 --> 21:21.090
I won't be able to see him again?

21:21.590 --> 21:22.220
Yeah.

21:24.050 --> 21:25.600
He's not anywhere?

21:27.970 --> 21:30.770
That's what death is about.

21:34.650 --> 21:35.900
I see.

21:35.900 --> 21:36.690
Yes.

21:51.290 --> 21:56.130
Shigofumi

21:51.290 --> 21:56.130
Episode Ten

21:51.290 --> 21:56.130
Encounter

23:26.930 --> 23:28.300
So kind.

23:28.800 --> 23:30.220
So warm.

23:31.220 --> 23:32.430
Tranquillity is sin.

23:33.390 --> 23:35.230
Intimate talk is punishment.

23:36.480 --> 23:37.810
Next time on Shigofumi:

23:38.980 --> 23:40.070
Awakening.

23:39.400 --> 23:41.400
Shigofumi

23:39.400 --> 23:41.400
Episode Eleven

23:39.400 --> 23:41.400
Awakening
